{"type": "step", "ts": 1793194356.532, "step": "critic", "status": "done", "attempt": 1, "stats": {"model": "nvidia/Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL", "label": "Super VL", "latency_s": 2.41, "tokens_in": 1452, "tokens_out": 403, "cost_usd": 0.000798, "calls": 1}, "data": {"evidence": "The arm grasped the red cube at t=2.3s, carried it to the blue cube, and released it at t=4.6s with the red cube center at [0.348, 0.0, 0.031], bottom only 0.6 cm above the floor. The final measured state shows the red cube is 8.2 cm off-center from the blue cube and 5.8 cm too low, i.e. it sits beside the blue cube on the floor rather than stacked on top.", "category": "wrong_placement", "what_happened": "The place step used the same zero-offset target as the pick step (blue_cube + [0,0,0]), so the gripper opened at floor level next to the blue cube instead of above it. The red cube was therefore released at z\u22480.031 m (cube bottom on the floor) instead of z\u22480.075 m (on top of the 0.05 m blue cube), and the lateral offset left it 8.2 cm away from the blue cube center.", "root_cause": "Place target was not offset upward by one cube height and was not aligned to the blue cube center; the plan treated the place pose identically to the pick pose.", "suggested_fix": "Change the place waypoint to blue_cube + [0.0, 0.0, 0.05] (gripper above the blue cube center, one cube height higher) and open the gripper there; optionally add a small approach/retract offset. This places the red cube bottom at z\u22480.075 m, centered on the blue cube, within the 2.5 cm horizontal and \u00b11.5 cm height tolerances."}}
